    "definition": "Acceptance targets, not measurements. Command handshake to done_valid includes state RAM and nominal ROM responses; pair covers both sources and shared paired filter. Excess ROM stalls and done backpressure count in total frame wall time. All launch/ramp/loop modes obey the same bound."
  },
  "protocol": {
    "handshake": "Rising clk with valid && ready; source holds valid and payload until accepted; no combinational ready->valid dependency",
    "commands": "One outstanding command including done response. cfg has priority over cmd at idle. cmd_pair requires even cmd_voice <=62 and pairRole/structure 2..10; scheduler derives this from independently maintained state. Single advances exactly one physical voice.",
    "frame": "cmd_frame is pre-step sampleClock, shared across all voices. Scheduler clears accepted/blocked once at frame start, chains actual done IRQ context into next command, then increments clock once after all voices. Core echoes frame unchanged.",
    "config": "One outstanding cfg response. Reads/writes use named state words; writes mask to field width; response returns post-write value. Accessible only when ready and no command is pending; a new configuration may be accepted on the same clock that the preceding response is consumed, permitting one write per clock. A stalled response blocks new configuration. Used for initial seeding, explicit external events, and assertion reads, never expected-state repair.",
    "rom": "CS plus banked byte offset after physical bus alignment, in exact reference order. One outstanding request, response accepted no earlier than next edge after request. Response is decoded ROM byte; responder returns zero for unmapped/out-of-range access. No speculative, repeated, skipped or reordered reads. Mapping remains stable throughout command.",
    "completion": "State writes finish before done_valid. Result and IRQ context stable while !done_ready. done_source_owner/partner pack final waveControl[19:0] in bits 39:20 and sampleCurrent[19:0] in bits 19:0 for state-derived prefetch; non-pair partner is zero. Backpressure causes no further source/parameter/state update; next command only after response handshake.",
    "reset": "Synchronous active-high rst cancels all transactions and response valids. On deassertion scrub 512 rows of all eight banks in parallel, holding ready/cmd_ready/cfg_ready low. ready rises after zeroing. Responder cancels outstanding reads on same rst; stale responses prohibited. Scheduler resets sampleClock and IRQ context; physical ROM mappings persist. Parameter fault and hook transaction are cancelled on rst.",
    "stalls": "Unbounded external stall is legal for numerical correctness but cannot pass realtime acceptance. Count all excess ROM request/response wait cycles and done stalls against frame reserve; no timeout dropping samples.",
    "parameters": "PS supplies one hook packet containing the SC88PAR1 delta and optional terminal candidate, or mask=0 no-op. Fixed 22 u32 lanes, inactive lanes ignored. Packet carries absolute pre-step frame, physical voice and stage 1..4. Early valid waits for the actual hook; valid/payload held through backpressure. Stage 1/2 after non-audio launch transition, stage 3 after source advance when running counter reaches 6, then stage 4 on every running source. Incoming combinedAmp is smoothed before any hook. Wrong frame/voice/stage/mask/width/terminal reason latches param_fault until reset, advances no parameter fields and produces no completion. Missing/late packets stall without repeating source or TVA; scheduler deadline reports underrun. Duplicate packet is rejected at the next hook by identity. Ramp hold bit17 remains local. Armed unmasked candidates arbitrate after Mute/Loop using actual IRQ; only successful delivery sets hold. No phase/FIFO/DPCM/filter/TVA or golden IRQ payload."
  },
